ella_csm: FYI onboarding call with Reachify, their Cloudflare Worker integration is hitting intermittent 429s during SDK init. sending logs shortly.
ricardo_cs_pm: Account ID? plan (hosted/dedicated)? any SLA ask from them?
ella_csm: acct: reachify-prod, on Hosted tier for now. They spin up ~30 worker instances that all call our preflight /v1/sessions at coldstart. Getting bursts of 429s after a few minutes.
jon_eng_sre: thanks. likely a thundering herd on preflight. can you paste one of the failing responses/headers? Check for Retry-After or X-RateLimit headers.
ella_csm: here's a sample response body they sent: ```{"error":"rate_limited","message":"too many preflight requests"}``` No Retry-After header in their captures.
maya_devex: common pattern for edge workers: every invocation fetches a fresh ephemeral token and hits preflight. suggest client-side splay + local token cache. also add an instance-id header so we can correlate traffic per-worker.
sam_eng_infra: also add: CF Workers have dynamic outbound IPs -> our per-IP heuristics can overcount. we treat many connections from varied IPs as high QPS. we can relax heuristics for this account temporarily.
jon_eng_sre: can you share a minimal repro snippet from the worker? that will help us reproduce in lab.
ella_csm: sample fetch from customer: ```
addEventListener('fetch', event => {
  event.respondWith(handle(event.request))
})

async function handle(req) {
  const token = await fetch('https://auth.reachify.com/ephemeral').then(r=>r.text())
  const res = await fetch('https://api.redwood.ai/v1/sessions', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`,
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      'x-client': 'reachify-worker'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({runtime: 'edge'})
  })
  return res
}
```
jon_eng_sre: perfect. two quick asks: 1) can they cache the token in global scope for N seconds to avoid per-invocation auth calls? 2) add jitter (random 0-300ms) before preflight when bootstrapping many instances. both will drastically reduce fanout.
maya_devex: here's a tiny SDK patch we can give them to debounce calls (pseudocode): ```
// global scope
let _cachedToken = null
let _tokenExpiry = 0
async function getToken() {
  if (Date.now() < _tokenExpiry && _cachedToken) return _cachedToken
  const t = await fetch('/auth/ephemeral')
  _cachedToken = await t.text()
  _tokenExpiry = Date.now() + 45000 // 45s
  return _cachedToken
}

async function preflight() {
  await sleep(Math.random()*250)
  const token = await getToken()
  return fetch('/v1/sessions', { headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` } })
}
```
ricardo_cs_pm: thanks Maya — I'll send that snippet + recommended headers to Reachify before the call. also mention we can temporarily bump their preflight quota.
ella_csm: customer confirmed they can change code. scheduling screenshare in 20m to walk through patch.
jon_eng_sre: I'll reproduce in staging with CF worker env and run 100 parallel coldstarts. quick note: if we don't see Retry-After, our rate-limiter is returning synthetic 429s from the IP-heuristic tier. I'll add debug flags to logs so we can see which limiter tripped.
sam_eng_infra: I'll also open a short-lived exception: relax per-ip counting for acct=reachify-prod for 6h. if all looks fine we can extend.
deploy-bot: rate-limit-exception created (#EXC-8123) by sam_eng_infra, expires in 6h.
jon_eng_sre: added log hook: set header X-Redwood-Limiter: preflight-ip-heuristic in failing responses (staging only). ela: ask them to repro and paste failing response headers during call.
ella_csm: will do. I'll capture full request/response headers live. thanks team, will update thread after screenshare. :raised_hands:
